[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 377,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 176,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57425,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 176,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leiomyoma is a benign tumour of smooth muscle.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 378,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 177,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57426,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 177,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8890/0 Leiomyoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 379,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 178,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57427,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 178,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2F30.Y &amp; XH4CY6 Other specified benign neoplasm of breast &amp; Leiomyoma NOS</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 380,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 179,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57428,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 179,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 381,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 180,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57429,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 180,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Superficial:</em> cutaneous (pilar) leiomyoma, leiomyoma of the nipple/areola (muscularis mamillae and areolae).</p>\r\n<p><em>Deep:</em> leiomyoma of the breast parenchyma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 382,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 181,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57430,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 181,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Leiomyoma can be localized in the dermis (cutaneous leiomyoma), the nipple/areola, or the breast parenchyma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 383,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 182,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57431,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 182,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients may be asymptomatic or present with pain or a palpable nodule/mass without specific imaging features {21416339; 24898199}. Multiple tumours occur rarely.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 384,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 183,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57432,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 183,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients are women {17709693}. The age range is broad, from 20&nbsp;to 70&nbsp;years, with an average age of 43&nbsp;years.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 385,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 184,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57433,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 184,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A few cases have been reported in association with the syndrome of hereditary leiomyomatosis and renal cell carcinoma, which is attributable to germline mutation of <em>FH</em> (encoding fumarate hydratase) {28288038; 11865300}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 386,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 185,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57434,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 185,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 393,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 206,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57435,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 206,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In contrast to the poorly defined superficial lesions, deep (parenchymal) lesions are well circumscribed. The neoplasms are firm, rubbery, and grey to tan, with a whorled cut surface. Superficial lesions are commonly smaller than deep-seated ones {17709693}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 387,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 186,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57436,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 186,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The histopathology and immunophenotype of these lesions are identical to those of smooth muscle tumours elsewhere in the body {2467872; 28751104; 16848853; 532847; 1879812}. Leiomyoma of the skin or nipple/areolar region shows, in association with the pilar muscle or muscularis mamillae/areolae, a poorly defined disorganized increase in smooth muscle bundles, which can be confluent. The spindle cells have elongated cigar-shaped nuclei and eosinophilic cytoplasm. Focal degenerative cytological atypia may be seen, but mitotic figures are absent. Lesions within the parenchyma are (multi)nodular and well circumscribed. They consist of intersecting fascicles of elongated smooth muscle cells with or without slight degenerative atypia. Mitotic activity is usually absent or low. Oedema and hyalinization may be present. Immunohistochemical markers (SMA and desmin) may be used to confirm a smooth muscle phenotype. Loss of expression of fumarate hydratase by immunohistochemistry may suggest the diagnosis of hereditary leiomyomatosis and renal cell carcinoma in the rare familial cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 388,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 187,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57437,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 187,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 389,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 188,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57438,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 188,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 392,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 191,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57439,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 191,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> tumour composed of cells with smooth muscle differentiation; absence of atypia and substantial mitotic activity.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 390,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 189,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57440,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 189,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 391,
    "bookid": 32,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 190,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 57441,
        "bookId": 32,
        "chapterId": 76,
        "headingId": 190,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Excision is the treatment of choice. Recurrences are rare {28751104; 17709693; 1879812}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2019-09-03T14:31:50"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]